From aad95485ecf087eecb2733201798bf6fa27c8dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brodi Elwood <brodielwood@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 22:14:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] plugins/screencast: fix type confusion between DRM fourcc and
 SPA video format

When the consumer sends a format choice (SPA_FORMAT_VIDEO_format
property) in its param update, ScreenCastStream::onStreamParamChanged
checks whether the current m_drmFormat is still in the offered list:

    std::span<const spa_video_format> values(...);
    if (reallocationRequired || !std::ranges::contains(values, m_drmFormat)) {

m_drmFormat is a DRM fourcc (e.g. AR24 = 0x34325241) but values are
spa_video_format enum entries (e.g. BGRA = 12). The two value spaces
never overlap, so std::ranges::contains is always false, the body is
always entered, m_drmFormat is 'changed' to the same value the consumer
already asked for, pw_stream_update_params is called, and pipewire
fires onStreamParamChanged again with the same format choice. Infinite
renegotiation; zero frames delivered until the consumer eventually
times out.

This is reproducible with Sunshine on a hybrid Intel+NVIDIA system
where CUDA can't import the iGPU's tiled DMA-BUF: pipewire negotiation
falls through the modifier branch into the format branch, which then
loops at full CPU speed for several seconds. Setups where the modifier
branch resolves (Ethan Lee's report in !8293 comment 23, OBS on a
single-GPU system) never reach this code path and don't notice the
bug.

Convert each advertised spa_video_format to its DRM fourcc before
comparing against m_drmFormat.

Source-Commit: 38b534402dc9dd91d7625d6073aae53680cbcfdd
Target-Version: KWin v6.8.0 with rebased upstream HDR MRs
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp b/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
index 8adabae84fbb328ee8ae5550c07cd947f952b952..024f3a9a5bfaf2d44a9c8ba48682aec79a9b2242 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
@@ -349,7 +349,17 @@ void ScreenCastStream::onStreamParamChanged(uint32_t id, const struct spa_pod *f
         }
     } else if (auto formatProperty = spa_pod_find_prop(format, nullptr, SPA_FORMAT_VIDEO_format)) {
         std::span<const spa_video_format> values((spa_video_format *)SPA_POD_CHOICE_VALUES(&formatProperty->value), SPA_POD_CHOICE_N_VALUES(&formatProperty->value));
-        if (reallocationRequired || !std::ranges::contains(values, m_drmFormat)) {
+        // m_drmFormat is a DRM fourcc (e.g. AR24=0x34325241); values are
+        // spa_video_format enum entries (e.g. BGRA=12). Comparing the two
+        // directly never matches, so the body would always be entered and
+        // m_drmFormat would be "changed" to the same value on every
+        // callback — an infinite renegotiation loop with consumers that
+        // send a format choice in their param. Convert each spa entry to
+        // its DRM fourcc first.
+        const bool currentFormatStillOffered = std::ranges::any_of(values, [this](spa_video_format spaFormat) {
+            return spaVideoFormatToDrmFormat(spaFormat) == m_drmFormat;
+        });
+        if (reallocationRequired || !currentFormatStillOffered) {
             // attempt to change the format to something the client supports
             const auto supported = Compositor::self()->backend()->supportedFormats();
             for (spa_video_format spaFormat : values) {
